    "diagnosis": "BIOMASS_ABOVE_READING",
    "late_biomass_estimate_od": 1.9,
    "p_biomass_above_reading": 0.98,
    "rationale": "Undiluted readings plateau at about 0.5 from 4 h onward. The 18 h aliquot read 0.193 at 10x dilution (two replicates, 0.189 and 0.198), which scales to about 1.9. A 50x dilution read 0.033, which scales to about 1.65, but it is near the low end of the reader's range and is noisier. Both are far above the undiluted 0.506, so the reader is saturating and the plateau is an artefact. The 4 h aliquot also read higher when diluted (0.0594 at 10x, scaling to 0.59, against 0.48 undiluted), so saturation starts at about 0.5. The true late biomass is therefore about 1.7–2 OD units, not about 0.5."
  },
